## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses handling of articulated, hinge-based objects in clutter, real-time constraints, and on-device adaptation with few shots.

## Key Concepts

- Articulated 6-DoF pose estimation for hinged objects
- Hinge-state (open/closed) inference
- Synthetic+real data with domain adaptation
- Few-shot on-device fine-tuning
- Real-time edge deployment considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pose error metric example (illustrative)
function poseError(est, gt) {
  // est/gt: {R: rotation matrix, t: translation vector}
  const rotError = rotationDistance(est.R, gt.R);
  const transError = vectorDistance(est.t, gt.t);
  return { rotError, transError };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you mitigate pose ambiguity from symmetric trays?
- How would you extend to add new hinge geometries online without retraining a large model?
